whoever said that rules were made to be  broken never danced under Abby Lee  Miller's watchful eye here are ten of  the most unbelievable rules the cast of  Dance Moms was made to follow catch on  quick or else it's no secret that  growing up on the set of Dance Moms can  be super stressful Nia Maddie Mackenzie  and Chloe have all posted YouTube videos  explaining just how active their lives  used to be not the studio every second  despite Dance Moms being a reality TV  show there were many instances where the  girls were instructed to fake it till  they make it during a tell-all vlog Nia  revealed that a not-so-secret Dance Moms  rule went along the lines of catch on  quick or get out of the studio the girls  had a very limited amount of time to  learn their dance routines  despite the show making it seem like  they had an entire week to do this in  reality they usually had anywhere  between a few hours to a few days tops  but they were expected to catch on quick  or face the consequences no makeup no  dancing it's totally normal for parents  to want to stop their young girls from  wearing makeup before they reach a  suitable age but if you're planning on  becoming a dance mom you'll have to  reconsider your morals Abby Lee wants  all the girls to have a fresh face of  makeup whenever the cameras are around  no matter how young they are she wants  everyone to look their best and that's a  rule you can't ignore failing to wear  makeup while being filmed will set  Abby's nerves sky-high and you don't  want to mess with Abby when she's angry  the pyramid rule every day is Mamas fan  knows a thing or two about pyramid day  and they also know that there's no  escaping it  being present on pyramid day was a must  and it forced the girls to be  scrutinized while one dancers abilities  were praised Maddie failed to attend the  dreadful weekly events could result in a  contract breach which simply wasn't an  option to make matters worse the girls  were made to stand straight throughout  the entire ordeal which was super  uncomfortable  actually it's for standing up straight  for a few hours while being criticized  is something we never want to do still  the last rule on this list makes the  pyramid rule sound like a breeze dance  mom rules  the dancers weren't the only ones being  watched though because their mothers  also had a little rulebook to follow if  they signed to the Dance Moms contract  they were basically agreeing to forego  their careers and become a full-time  dance mom on top of that the mothers had  to respect Abby's studio time they could  watch from afar but they weren't  supposed to enter the studio when Abby  was teaching but of course not every  single dance mom was going to respect  this rule especially when they could see  Abby yelling at their kids for no  apparent reason but if there's one rule  every dance mom learned relatively  quickly it was to never question Abby  Lee Miller because well they would live  to regret it no school on Fridays to say  that the girls had a wildly hectic  schedule would be an understatement we  have two trios and a group dance dancing  came first and school came second which  wasn't exactly ideal many of the girls  had to stop attending public school and  resort to being tutored across the  street from Abby Lee's dance studio but  not all of them wanted to sever ties  with their schools and friends so many  of them juggled public school and  professional dancing at the same time  but there was a catch the girls weren't  allowed to go to school on Fridays  because well Fridays were left open for  competitions their rituals  believe it or not but the dancers had a  self-inflicted rule that could not be  ignored while it wasn't exactly appease  doing the girls became incredibly  superstitious during their time on Dance  Moms  according to Nia if the girls didn't do  their special handshake before  performing the number they would totally  butcher their performance they also  believed in jinxes which led them to  knock on wood and perform small rituals  whenever they attempted their faith  these rules were taken very seriously  despite not being an Abby Lee Miller's  contract no piercings no tattoos every  dance studio has its own set of rules an  Abby Lee Miller is no exception not  being allowed to have facial piercings  sounds pretty reasonable  after all judges do look at a dancers  overall image when giving a verdict  however Abby Lee was a lot stricter than  the average person  according to Chloe wearing piercings of  any kind was absolutely forbidden and so  was getting tattoos while these rules  didn't impact the girls during their  junior years it's safe to say that  became annoying once they were teenagers  according  to a be wearing jewelry can be dangerous  but still what's the harm in wearing  studded earrings prim and proper Abby  Lee Miller wants her dancers to be prim  and proper at all times she wants them  to be completely natural with the  exception of makeup of course her  dancers are required to have their hair  up in the studio and failing to do so  can get them kicked out in a jiffy  just ask Chloe perhaps the most  important role the girls have to follow  is keeping their hair completely natural  dyeing your hair getting highlights or  putting some funky colors in it is  forbidden yet somehow Jojo was still  allowed on the show did you guys know  that JoJo's mom has been bleaching her  daughter's hair since she was a kid  it looks like Abby chose to let that one  slide no tears no complaining it's old  news that Abby Lee Miller has little to  no patience and an extreme hatred for  crybabies according to her being yelled  at and ridiculed isn't a good enough  reason for children to cry all in all  Abby is super ruthless and hates  complainers Abby has a bunch of rules  listed on the ALDC official page and one  of them states that dancers should come  to class with ambition energy and a  positive attitude we don't know about  you but that seems like a lot to ask  three-year-olds and emotional preteens  though wait role it's totally normal for  dance studios to have some pretty  atrocious rules but the weight rule  simply takes the cake Chloe was one of  the few girls to refuse to sign Abby's  contract due to how ridiculous it was it  said that the girls weren't allowed to  gain or lose 5 to 10 pounds and had to  sign away 10% of their earnings Chloe  refused to do this and wasn't allowed on  the show for the beginning of season 4  can you imagine telling your little girl  to monitor her weight if she intends to  continue dancing at ALDC yeah we didn't  think so  so which dance moms rule did you find  the most ridiculous let us know in the  comment section below thanks for  watching the things for more videos like  this one hit that subscribe button and  don't forget to give this video a big  thumbs up we'll see you next time  [Music]
 

